title: A clone of a config repo works only with 'main' checked out and an author set in each submodule, and with every foreign skgrepo its configs name present beside it.
pid: 9cf082ba-010a-4734-a5e4-5a234eeda9ad
body: |2-
  Tested on a clone made with '--recurse-submodules' from local bare
  copies. A cloned submodule sits at its pin with no branch, and has
  none of the original's local Git config, so skg's commit fails with
  "no git author is configured". The server refuses a config whose
  foreign skgrepo path is missing ("Invalid skg config ... path does not
  exist"), so claude-config needs Jeff's 'data/jeff/' beside it, and
  his needs ours. A local test clone also needs
  'git -c protocol.file.allow=always', which GitHub URLs do not.
